{"availability":"available","full":"Bubbler-4/TryInBrowser","name":"TryInBrowser","description":"Online interpreter that works even if you go offline","category":"Other","language":"Rust","stars":4,"forks":0,"created":"2021-06-03T06:15:25Z","updated":"2021-08-18T10:17:25Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://try-in-browser.netlify.app/","topics":["online-interpreter","rust","wasm","webassembly"],"demo":"https://try-in-browser.netlify.app/","color":"#63362a","ink":"#f8c7a8","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:48.808Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:48.808Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:48.808Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-10T21:05:48.808Z","stars":4,"forks":0}],"technologies":["Rust"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Online interpreter that works even if you go offline","Most online interpreters require a server to run the submitted programs. And making different runs not interfere with each other (security concerns aside) is difficult.","Try In Browser attempts to solve this problem by moving all the interpreters into the browser. No need to isolate runs. No need to run a dedicated server; a simple file server (such as GitHub Pages) is enough. An added benefit is that, once everything is loaded, you can disconnect from the Internet and still use it."],"features":[],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Bubbler-4/TryInBrowser/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"d7f23490d319c648a757f34ae665d173e5f02826354e78e5141f491a9372324b","extractedAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:49.009Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:49.009Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Online interpreter that works even if you go offline","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Bubbler-4/TryInBrowser/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"d7f23490d319c648a757f34ae665d173e5f02826354e78e5141f491a9372324b","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Bubbler-4/TryInBrowser/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-10T21:05:49.009Z"},"overviewRe